# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
version: "0.1.0~alpha1"
synopsis: "Deterministic CBOR for hash-bearing protocols"
description: """
RFC 8949 CBOR with a permissive decoder and a strict encoder, offering both
the RFC 8949 section 4.2.1 and the RFC 7049 section 3.9 map orderings, and
reporting the source byte span of every decoded value so that a structure
identified by the hash of its encoding can be re-hashed from the bytes it
arrived in rather than from a re-encode.

No bignum dependency: arbitrary-precision integers are carried as magnitudes
and never operated on, so this links into a unikernel without GMP."""
maintainer: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
authors: ["Gil Bahat <bahat.gil@gmail.com>"]
license: "ISC"
homepage: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-web3-codec"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-web3-codec/issues"
depends: [
  "dune" {>= "3.0"}
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "alcotest" {with-test}
  "qcheck-core" {with-test}
  "qcheck-alcotest" {with-test}
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  ["dune" "subst"] {dev}
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/reuna-labs/ocaml-web3-codec.git"
